@node Features
@chapter Features

@cindex Features

Remote control the Triode app from Emacs:

@itemize
@item
Choose station
@item
Play/Stop toggle
@item
Mute toggle
@item
Copy current station and track to clipboard
@item
Recognize music with Shazam
@item
Open Triode app
@end itemize

@node Requirements
@chapter Requirements

@cindex Requirements


@strong{triode.el} requires the following programs and Elisp packages:

@itemize
@item
macOS 15+ (Sequoia)  

@item
GNU Emacs 30.1+ (@ref{Top,,,emacs,})

@item
@uref{https://triode.app, Triode app} for macOS 2.4+

@item
@uref{https://github.com/kickingvegas/restlib, restlib} 0.1+

@item
@uref{https://github.com/kickingvegas/shazam, shazam.el} 0.1+
@end itemize

@node Install
@chapter Install

@cindex Install
@vindex triode-init

For manual installation@comma{} ensure that @code{triode.el} is available in the Emacs @code{load-path} variable.

This package requires the installation of a macOS Shortcut named “Triode RC JSON”. Download and install it in your library of Shortcuts by clicking on the link below:

@itemize
@item
@uref{https://www.icloud.com/shortcuts/0db0f47809fe4b0a84ac640846fd65ee, iCloud Shortcut: Triode RC JSON}
@end itemize

@strong{triode.el} by default requires your Emacs session to load the macOS SF Symbols font. Use the convenience function @code{triode-init} to setup both SF Symbols and to globally set your keybinding preference to the @code{triode-tmenu} command in your Emacs initialization file.

@lisp
(require 'triode) ;; optional if autoloaded
(triode-init "<f14>")
@end lisp

The use of the keybinding @kbd{<f14>} is merely a suggestion and can be changed to preference.

@node Usage
@chapter Usage

@cindex Usage
@vindex triode-tmenu
@vindex triode-dismiss-menu-for-actions


@image{images/triode-tmenu,,,,png}

Invoke the Transient menu @code{triode-tmenu} via @code{execute-extended-command} (@kbd{<f14>}) or by your preferred keybinding.

@example
M-x triode-tmenu RET
@end example


@code{triode-tmenu} offers the following menu items

@table @asis
@item @kbd{s}
Select station - open Triode app station selector to choose an internet radio station from your favorites list.

@item @kbd{@key{SPC}}
Play/Stop toggle to connect or disconnect to an internet radio station.

@item @kbd{m}
Muting toggle. This command does not disconnect an already connected internet radio station.

@item @kbd{r}
Refresh Triode app state (station@comma{} current track@comma{} playback state).

@item @kbd{w}
Copy current track to the clipboard (@code{kill-ring}).

@item @kbd{z}
Open @code{Shazam} music recognition. This requires @code{shazam.el} to be installed.

@item @kbd{o}
Open Triode app.

@item @kbd{@comma{}}
Open @code{triode.el} settings.

@item @kbd{@key{RET}}
Dismiss menu.
@end table

By default@comma{} most of the commands in @code{triode-tmenu} will keep the menu displayed. This behavior can be changed with setting the customizable variable @code{triode-dismiss-menu-for-actions} to @code{t}.

