@node Triode State Polling
@section Triode State Polling

@cindex Triode State Polling
@vindex triode-start-polling-status
@vindex triode-cancel-polling
@vindex triode-poll-status-interval

By default@comma{} @code{triode.el} will synchronize state between Emacs and the Triode app whenever a user action is taken. However@comma{} internet radio stations routinely can change metadata state (current track). While the Triode app can keep track of such changes@comma{} there is no capability for it to message such changes to Emacs.

A workaround is to have @strong{triode.el} periodically poll the Triode app to synchronize state. The following commands to support this are:

@deffn Command triode-start-polling-status
Start polling to synchronize Triode app state.
@end deffn

@deffn Command triode-cancel-polling
Stop polling to synchronize Triode app state.
@end deffn

The polling period is defined by the customizable variable @code{triode-poll-status-interval} (default 200 seconds).

